<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf al-Azma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf al-Azma was a Syrian army officer and war minister of the Arab Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Trained in the Ottoman army, he refused to accept the French ultimatum of July 1920 without a fight and led a small force against the French at Maysalun, where he was killed on 24 July 1920. He is honoured in Syria as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yusuf-al-azma.jpg" alt="Yusuf al-Azma" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yusuf_al-Azma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
